_3D.AniGravityMode [SimTalk]
Activates Gravity Mode of the length-oriented object designated by <Path> (true) or deactivates it
(false).
Remarks
This setting only applies to the length-oriented objects. It is especially helpful for suspension tracks, etc.
Gravity Mode only affects automatic animations, that is animations for which you did not specify an
animation path.
On a suspension track the part is always placed perpendicular to the floor in Gravity Mode, either hanging
from a rail on the ceiling or standing up on a rail on the floor.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>._3D.AniGravityMode:boolean
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type boolean.
Example
MyConveyor._3D.AniGravityMode := true
See also
Gravity Mode
_3D.AniGravityMode [SimTalk]
12-766 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

_3D.AnimationOffset [SimTalk]
Sets the Animation Offset of the length-oriented object designated by <Path>.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>._3D.AnimationOffset:length[3]
Assignment Value
You can assign an array of data type length with three values.
The values set the offset of the animation path to the surface of the object along the X-direction, the
Y-direction, and the Z-direction.
Example
MyConveyor._3D.AnimationOffset := [0m, 0m, 1m]
See also
Animation Offset
_3D.AnimationOffset [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 12-767
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

_3D.AniSmoothRotation [SimTalk]
Activates Smooth Rotation of the length-oriented object designated by <Path> (true) or deactivates it
(false).
Remarks
This setting only applies to the length-oriented objects. It is especially helpful for suspension tracks, etc.
Smooth Rotation only affects automatic animations, that is animations for which you did not specify an
animation path.
If the object currently animates its MUs using a user-defined Animation Path Type > Lines, Smooth
Rotation specifies whether the part slowly changes its rotation around the anchor points (like this is the
case on a Station (true) for example) or if it abruptly changes its orientation (like at a corner on a
Conveyor with the standard MU animation) (false).
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>._3D.AniSmoothRotation:boolean
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type boolean.
Example
MyConveyor._3D.AniSmoothRotation := true
See also
Smooth Rotation
_3D.AniSmoothRotation [SimTalk]
12-768 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

_3D.BaseHeight [SimTalk] - 3D
Sets the Base Height of the length-oriented object designated by <Path>.
Remarks
The Base Height sets the distance between the insertion height (z-coordinate) of the length-oriented
object and the height of a segment whose ΔZ equals 0.
Base height 1 meter Base height 2 meters
The Base Height can be inherited, meaning that you can define it once in the class instead of having to
define it for each instance individually. The z-coordinate defines the floor of the installation and the base
height defines the distance of the legs from the floor. By changing the setting ΔZ in the Segments Table,
you can add an additional offset.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>._3D.BaseHeight:length
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type length.
Example
MyConveyor._3D.BaseHeight := 3
print MyConveyor._3D.BaseHeight
See also
Base Height [tab Appearance]
_3D.BaseHeight [SimTalk] - 3D
Plant Simulation Help 12-769
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

