_3D.ExtConfiguration [SimTalk]
Sets the extrusion configuration of the length-oriented object designated by <Path>.
Remarks
An example of an extrusion configuration might look like this:
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>._3D.ExtConfiguration:table
Parameters of the Extrusion Configuration
The parameters of the extrusion configuration designate the following settings:
• Index Name: Is the name of the extrusion group, it is only entered once for each group in the first
column of the group, i.e., in column 0.
• Extrusion Profile: The subtable [2 x number of points], which you can open by double-clicking in the
cell Extrusion Profile, specifies the profile that will be extruded according to the settings below. Define
the values in a way so that they match a width of 1 meter.
• Configuration Type: You can set the following values:
_3D.ExtConfiguration [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 12-771
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Name/Value for
Assignment Description
Path, z max, Move
abs/0
Extrude once along the path with z as defined in the anchors, the distance from
the edge remains fixed when changing the width.
Path, z max, Move
rel/1
Extrude once along the path with z as defined in the anchors and pin the profile
base point to its relative position when changing the width.
Path, z max, Scale
x/2
Extrude once along the path with z as defined in the anchors and scale in the
x-direction when changing the width.
Path, z max, Scale
xy/3
Extrude once along the path with z as defined in the anchors and scale in the
x-direction and the y-direction when changing the width.
Path, Floor, Move
abs/4
Extrude once along the path with z = 0.0, the distance from the edge remains
fixed when changing the width.
Path, Floor, Move
rel/5
Extrude once along the path with z = 0.0 and pin the profile base point to its
relative position when changing the width.
Path, Floor, Scale
